Package: pckz-audio-switcher
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: pckz contributors <maintainers@pckz.invalid>
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Depends: libgtk-4-1 (>= 4.14), libadwaita-1-0 (>= 1.7), pulseaudio-utils
Recommends: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator, bluez
Description: Sound device switcher for the tray, PulseAudio and PipeWire
 Switch the default output and input from the top bar or a small window,
 exactly like GNOME Settings does (card profiles and ports included):
 HDMI/DisplayPort monitors by name, Bluetooth speakers and headsets
 (connecting paired ones on click), USB headsets, webcams, S/PDIF, and
 virtual devices — each with its own icon. Includes per-device volume,
 card configuration and per-application volume.
 .
 The tray starts automatically for every user; on GNOME it needs the
 AppIndicator extension (enabled by default on Ubuntu).
